Since April the desk merged **412 reports** into #4471 and called it one issue. The merged
data holds **two different bugs** with two different fixes, and the second is not a duplicate.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

<Callout kind="warn">
`hint` is not a duplicate of `parser`. 33 reports from booking-v3 tenants, form channel only,
are a second problem. They need their own ticket.
</Callout>

## The two problems

- **`parser` — 379 reports.** The shared parser reads every date month first, while our
  tenants write the day first. Every tenant on file is day-first, so their app and email
  reports come out with the month and day swapped. One shared fix covers them all.
- **`hint` — 33 reports.** `booking-v3` prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field while the
  form reads the value `DD/MM/YYYY`. People type what the hint tells them, and the form reads
  the other order, so the date flips the other way. Only form reports from the three
  booking-v3 tenants: `alder.physio`, `copper.studio`, `pale.harbour`. The fix is the hint or
  the form, not the shared parser.

## Resolution (desk update, #4471 closed 05 Oct)

- **`parser` — fixed.** `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales` on the shared parser.
- **`hint` — won't fix.** The booking-v3 form was retired.

## Reports the desk read differently

`desk-notes.json` flags 5 reports the desk read as one-day moves, not month flips. By tenant
they sit inside `parser`, and the table above counts them there. They describe a day shift
(11 vs 12 May; "only June"; Lisbon vs Toronto), so the desk should keep watching them as a
possible separate problem, but they are not the shared parser bug.

